f44ce49f59c5fee5a90ebff03913082d163dee57"},{"name":"noise-arch_avfs_reviews.xml","source":"original","mtime":"1621648278","size":"2199","format":"Metadata","md5":"92dbef7447c77d9510a56e41f56f5a6e","crc32":"f4aca92b","sha1":"5198ea6097af212715cd8dd50ceb5e524f3b645a"}],"files_count":34,"item_last_updated":1621648283,"item_size":194114784,"metadata":{"identifier":"noise-arch_avfs","collection":["noise-arch","cassettetapes"],"date":"1987","description":"Side A\n1. Wigglepig - Glue Factory (2:43)\n2. The Company - Voices From The Plains Of Jars (6:22)\n3. Darren Copeland - The Three Faces (Mahwje-Daze-Dore)\t(9:32)\n4. Bones With Reverend Sermon - Distraction (1 Piece In 4 Movements) (2:15)\n5. Violence And The Sacred - Stürmisch Bewegt (12:30)\n6. Sucking Chest Wound\t - Wake Up... America (4:26)\n7. Catastrophe Theory - Day Rides A Tiger (4:14)\n\nSIde B\n1. Electro Static Cat - Seek Demersal Life (4:06)\n2. Abstract Gallery - John The Madman\t(3:25)\n3. Gerard Leckey - Ninety One (8:43)\n4. John Oswald - Robot Aggregates Experiment (Test #3) (3:00)\n5. Wende Bartley - Rising Tides Of Generations Lost (14:28)\n6. Bryan Ruryk - Osler Incident (1:09)\n7. Varoshi Fame - Ogamu (4:25)\n8. Particle Zoo - Untitled (4:52)","mediatype":"audio","scanner":"Internet Archive Python library 0.9.8","subject":"Cassette;Tape;Noise-Arch;Independent","title":"NOISE-ARCH Collection: A view From Somewhere","publicdate":"2015-12-03 00:10:00","uploader":"jscott@archive.org","addeddate":"2015-12-03 00:10:00","creator":"Myke Dyer","year":"1987","backup_location":"ia905506_3"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"There's a piece on side 2, reckon it must be Ninety One by Gerard Leckey that's fantastic, 8'43\" of great sound, nostalgia for an age yet to come!","reviewtitle":"The 80's were as radical as I remember","reviewer":"usine81","reviewdate":"2016-08-05 18:23:12","createdate":"2016-08-05 18:23:12","stars":"5"},{"reviewbody":"I mailed away and got this back in the 80s. Enjoyed it immensely back then. I even did a presentation for an english class in college, where this was a center piece. \n\nSeeing this slice of 80s experimental cassette culture up here is really nice. I hope that you keep expanding it.","reviewtitle":"Thank you John Doe!","reviewer":"edblake","reviewer_itemname":"@edblake","reviewdate":"2018-07-23 21:57:42","createdate":"2018-07-23 21:57:42","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"This is a standout compilation that showcases how unique and distinct cassette culture was. Every track is interesting in some way and the total listening experience is unique, like something unearthed from an alien planet. One of my very favorites in this collection.","reviewtitle":"Wow!","reviewer":"Mansion of Madness 89.3 FM KNON","reviewer_itemname":"@mansion_of_madness_89_3_fm_knon","reviewdate":"2019-06-24 15:53:27","createdate":"2019-06-24 15:53:27","stars":"5"},{"reviewtitle":"Fragments of Chalee","reviewbody":"Darren Copeland is so much better than Aaron Copeland. My g-d, this tape is amazing! ","stars":"5","reviewer":"skoalbandit","reviewdate":"2021-05-22 01:51:17","createdate":"2021-05-22 01:51:17","reviewer_itemname":"@skoalbandit"}],"server":"ia800503.us.archive.org","uniq":1415819395,"workable_servers":["ia800503.us.archive.org","ia600503.us.archive.org"]}